{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564559-your-average-hunter-cell-or-whatever-they-call-it-in-1st-edition","id":1564559,"title":"Your average hunter cell (or whatever they call it in 1st edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-06T05:52:52-07:00","id":1564559,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Your average hunter cell (or whatever they call it in 1st edition)","content":"I see no Hunter: The Reckoning sub on here so I assume this would be the best place since its possibly taking place in my VtM Chronicle.<br /> <br /> What's the expertise level of your average city based hunter cell? Currently my six man group ranges from an EMT and an ex combat vet to a 19 year old radioshack employee and a car mechanic.<br /> <br /> I'm also writing them as NPC's for the side plot I have planned but in choosing their Creeds I've made most of them Zeal based with no visionaries. This won't be much a of a problem right when they're all lost and clueless while beating up on the only Mercy based hunter......right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T09:54:57-07:00","id":1564565,"title":"","content":"There's no such a thing as an average Hunter cell. They're even more varied than Coteries or Packs, because the level of danger do make for strange bedfellows.<br /> <br /> You must consider a few things here:<br /> <br /> 1. Hunters with an actual fighting chance are over prepared. They may not know what their prey is capable of, but they know it is a lot and how dangerous not knowing is.<br /> <br /> 2. Any success, even a single Ghoul, raises the expertise of a hunter considerably. Their best asset isn't dots in the sheet, but practical knowledge of what can happen in the field.<br /> <br /> 3. The Messengers Imbue their charges during their first faceoff with the supernatural. Imbued are unlikely to be too na\u00efve. If you want rookie mistakes you're better off with regular hunters rather than Imbued.<br /> <br /> 4. Imbued only appeared in 1999. If the game is set earlier, what you want is an old excellent VtM book called <i>Hunter's Hunted</i>. In fact you can use it regardless of era or edition. You'll only have normal Hunters, but they may have some surprises in their sleeves if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T23:34:28-07:00","id":1564581,"title":"","content":"Using them as npcs I usually give them some knowledge of vampires, decently high dicepools (6-8) and have them apply decent tactics. <br /> <br /> You can get far with just making them run away quickly in a fight. They pop in, throw a molotov, headshots someone, drives away into the night, a pc is rotshrecking, another has a hole in his head, a third is trying to stop a crowd from noticing the other two guys, much humiliation, eternal vengeance sworn, good fun. <br /> <br /> I did once have a hunter attempt to recruit fresh ones which backfired as the new recruits were captured and interrogated and it ultimately led to her death, so I guess a varied amount of experience is the most fun.<br /> <br /> Feel like new recruits should be a massive danger to experienced hunters, but they are also very necessary to replenish the lost. Good source of friction. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T02:24:51-07:00","id":1564582,"title":"","content":"I think experienced hunters would learn quickly that any loss should be treated as the whole operation being compromised and be prepared to move. Doubly so with new recruits.<br /> <br /> But yes, that adds another important aspect of using hunters: don't try 'balance'. Hunters are minimally dangerous only as far as they're able to outsmart the monsters, which makes them quite dangerous.<br /> <br /> They're not that strong when caught, not even the Imbued, so any slip on their part is the end or at least a severe setback. And they're going to die, not simply take a beat and a wounded pride.<br /> <br /> Either you use them as a jumpscare or comedy interlude then discard, or you go for the throat and your PCs can seriously take serious hits if they're not ready.<br /> <br /> Your options to make this serious, but less lethal:<br /> <br /> 1. Give the hunters less lethal tactics. They still have a strategy, may be studying the targets or knowingly causing lasting harm without trying to finish your PCs off. Hit and run is indeed a very good option, but don't be mindless.<br /> <br /> 2. Give the PCs reason to not want the Hunters dead. Family ties, secrets, anything weird you can come up with, the PCs have good reason to think a permanent solution is actually worse. One option is they finding out something more genuinely dangerous will come out for them if the Hunters vanish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}